- op: discuss  # 38a6
  at: '2026-10-18T00:10:18Z'  # 38a6
  by: agent  # 38a6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 38a6
  clock: 3  # 38a6
  nonce: 38a6  # 38a6
  message: "Satisfied in PR #1702 (dev ac651f01d5). llvm_ir.py: the caller is the define at the call's recorded position (symbols_at); the callee is this file's define when it has one, the registry otherwise, and a local declare does not pre-empt another file's define. The never-read _pending_calls store is gone: Pass 1 extracts symbols only, Pass 2 collects calls (_collect_calls). Behavioral evidence: test_llvm_ir.py::TestLlvmIrEnclosingByPosition — two files each defining @foo keep their own calls (before: a.ll's foo -> b.ll's helper); @helper defined in both files binds to the same file's; a call to a function defined nowhere is dropped; the existing declare-in-main/define-in-utils case still resolves to the define."  # 38a6
